 "v1_problem": "CRM dispute tickets roughly doubled from a Jun-Jul baseline (~600/month) to 1180 (Aug) and 1260 (Sep) 2026 (E-06). This is not explained by slow ticket handling (median response 1.6d, p90 2.8d, within the 3.0d SLA — E-04) nor by a tariff change (zero logged changes — E-03). The majority of disputed bills (59%, 1,785/3,025) involve ACTUAL, not ESTIMATED, meter reads (E-02), which caps how much the confirmed field manual-read completion shortfall (88% vs 95% target, 9,200 accounts — E-01) can explain, since that mechanism only produces estimated bills. The best-supported remaining mechanism is a defect in billing import/validation processing of actual meter reads introduced around the same period, producing incorrect bills on actual-read accounts and driving the dispute surge (H-BILLING-RULE-CHANGE).",
 "v1_canonical": true,
 "v1_names_mechanism": true,
 "late_evidence_minute": 106.0,
 "challenge_detected": true,
 "redefine_qualified": false,
 "redefine_executed": true,
